			<div class="content" id="post-content-1295766">
									

<p>I quite like this. The previous installment I was somewhat ambivalent about, but this is good. There's a little of Jasper Fforde in there, but without the whimsy that can sometimes overpower JF's stories.</p>
<p>Nitpick/Question: Percival/Percy. The method of indicating speech by the character shifts in formality half-way through the card game - &quot;Percival said&quot;, &quot;Percival said&quot;, &quot;Percy sighed&quot;. Given the context in play, wouldn't it have a better consistency to have all the referential stuff informally, until (at least) the more formal greeting between Midnight and Percival?</p>
<p>Edit: Typo.</p>

							</div>

								
